WEBVTT

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:35.440
Then, you got more new cards?

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.090
Yes, two of them.

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:37.820
At home?

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.650
When Akiho-chan was over.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.610
What was she doing at the time?

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:47.160
She was asleep because of this.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.130
I see.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:51.610
I still didn't sense anything at all.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.860
Did you, Sakura-chan?

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:56.880
It was really faint,

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:59.320
but I could tell something was different.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:00.400
Different?

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:06.220
Even I'm not sure what, exactly, 
was different, but...

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:07.890
But it was different?

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:10.650
Yeah.

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:14.300
So right now, Sakura's the only 
one who can sense the cards.

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:18.440
Is this...

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.220
What is it, Tomoyo-chan?

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:23.810
Well, I might be mistaken, but...

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:27.050
Tell me. It might give me some kind of hint.

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:30.610
These cards, Labyrinth and Snooze,

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:37.200
seem to have similar powers as 
the Maze and Sleep Clow Cards.

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:45.060
<b>Sakura and the Upside-down Penguin</b>

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:50.070
Formulas are something you'll 
continue to use for a long time,

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:52.580
so make sure you memorize them.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.650
We'll start with equality.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.890
This means "equal to."

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:03.650
Formulas called "equalities" 
use it to express relationships

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:05.740
between numerical values.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:10.640
We call everything to its 
left the "left-side value,"

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:12.720
and to its right, the "right-side value."

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:16.490
The two sides put together are...

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:16.490
<i>It's like Tomoyo-chan said.</i>

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:21.000
<i>There are other cards that work 
a lot like the Clow Cards, too.</i>

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:25.820
<i>Aqua is similar to Watery,</i>

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:28.540
<i>Flight resembles Fly,</i>

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:32.190
<i>and Gale resembles Windy.</i>

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.940
<i>But would that mean...</i>

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:37.430
Kinomoto-san.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:39.560
Yes, sir!

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:47.090
So energetic. Did you doze off for a minute?

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:49.940
Oh, good.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:53.070
But I would like you to pay a 
bit more attention in class.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.470
Y-Yes, sir.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:04:00.040
Got it, Sensei...

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:07.070
I see... I guess you made yourself 
a little conspicuous.

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:10.830
I was so embarrassed.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:14.490
But you weren't really sleeping.

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:16.590
Still, I was spacing out.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:19.300
And in the middle of class...

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:20.850
Well, the weather's nice.

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:22.710
We all have days like that!

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:26.850
Sometimes, I get to thinking about 
a new story during class.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:31.190
And then the teacher calls on 
me, and I get flustered.

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:34.920
What kind of story are you 
thinking about now?

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:37.250
I'm still working on that.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:43.460
Oh, but our next play is going to 
be done mainly by first-years,

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:46.100
so I get to write the script.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.250
You're writing it?

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:50.640
Yeah. That's why I joined the Drama Club.

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:53.950
The Literature Club would've been good, too,

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:58.830
but I'm more interested in 
writing scripts than novels.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:01.590
Remember the album I showed you at my house?

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.140
From when you were a princess in a play?

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:05.780
R-Right...

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:08.910
Naoko-chan actually wrote 
the script for that play.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.150
What?

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:12.850
That's amazing, Naoko-san!

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:15.570
I'm still just studying...

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:18.130
Please show it to me, sometime!

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:20.570
S-Sure.

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:22.300
Sounds like we're having fun!

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.200
Sorry we're late.

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:29.510
Are you done talking to the teacher?

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:32.320
Yeah. It was about the next 
ball-sports tournament.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:35.560
Li-kun and I are on the operating committee.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.630
Oh, really?

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:39.820
It's fun, once you start doing the work.

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:44.390
But it's a little challenging to decide 
who'll be in which event.

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:45.680
Yeah.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:48.780
No one wants to be in an event 
they're not good at...

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:52.070
Which ball sport do you like, Akiho-chan?

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:55.050
Well, I've been playing 
tennis since I was little.

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:58.990
Oh, too bad. There's no 
tennis event, this time.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.880
What other events are there?

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:07.680
Volleyball, basketball, table tennis...

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:09.350
Oh, and badminton.

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:11.680
Too bad! It's so close to tennis, too!

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:12.670
Too bad?

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:14.590
Speaking of badminton...

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:18.260
It's a sport where two players 
stand on either side of a net

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:21.930
that's stretched across a court, and volley 
a shuttlecock to score points.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:26.240
It's actually in the Guinness Book 
as the world's fastest sport.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:30.450
Also, many people call it 
"batminton" by mistake,

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:33.620
but the correct name is "badminton."

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:38.580
Wait. I can't find anything 
to criticize in that.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:41.330
That was a very clear explanation!

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:45.460
Yamazaki-kun said something 
that wasn't a lie?

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.470
I tried going for the unexpected.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.220
This just doesn't feel right!

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:53.960
You're Yamazaki-kun! You're not 
supposed to tell the truth!

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.740
Do all three of you have the 
day off from your clubs?

00:06:58.740 --> 00:06:59.220
Yep.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.720
No cheerleading, today.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:04.340
And the Chorus Club is on 
break for piano tuning.

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:06.600
Plus, the teacher had some things to do.

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:11.100
There's a joint recital with another 
middle school next month,

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:13.250
so there was a meeting about that.

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:15.730
Can we go to the recital, too?

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:18.490
Yes, since it'll be in our auditorium.

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:20.530
You should come with us, Syaoran-kun.

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:21.260
Sure.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:24.640
I'll be looking forward to it, 
Tomoyo-chan, Akiho-chan.

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:25.370
Okay!

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:28.080
I'll practice lots and lots!

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:29.570
Akiho-san.

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:32.390
Kaito-san!

00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:34.900
Hello.

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:36.630
Hello!

00:07:38.170 --> 00:07:39.960
Are you on your way home?

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:42.090
Yes, and you?

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:43.990
I just finished some shopping.

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:45.610
I'll help you carry it!

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:47.870
Oh, no. I'm all right.

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:54.220
Forgive my rudeness. Hello.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:57.810
I take care of Akiho-sama.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:01.090
My name is Yuna D. Kaito.

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:02.940
I'm Syaoran Li.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:09.960
Akiho-san,

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:11.940
do you need to make any stops?

00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:13.080
No.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:14.850
Then, shall we head home?

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:17.230
Yes!

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.720
I hope you will both visit again soon.

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:23.720
And you, too, of course.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:32.930
So hungry...

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:37.340
Kero-chan!

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:40.100
I smelled yummy bread...

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:42.430
Because Kaito-san just bought some.

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:47.860
I couldn't come out when you were 
eatin' lunch, so I'm starvin' now...

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:51.140
Didn't I put snacks in there for you?

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:53.600
You know that ain't enough to hold me over!

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:55.690
Don't blame me if you get fat.

00:08:55.690 --> 00:09:00.090
A nice body, like mine, looks best 
with a little roundness to it.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:02.180
We're talking about a lot 
more than "a little"!

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:04.070
But that's why I'm so charming!

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:05.430
What's the matter?

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:19.450
<b>Eriol Hiiragizawa Calling</b>

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:21.680
<i>Good morning.</i>

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:24.950
<i>Actually, I suppose it's 
evening where you are.</i>

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:31.950
Someone with magical power is near Sakura?

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:37.810
<i>He's some sort of caretaker for the transfer 
student Sakura has befriended.</i>

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:39.460
What's his name?

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:41.470
<b>New Message</b>

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:41.470
<b>
Syaoran Li: 
Yuna D. Kaito</b>

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:43.270
Yuna... D.?

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:44.720
<i>Do you know him?</i>

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.720
Not on a personal basis,

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:52.310
but if the "D" refers to 
what I think it does...

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:54.730
<i>The "D"?</i>

00:09:57.460 --> 00:10:00.800
Here, in England, there's a magic association

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:04.230
that grants its highest-ranked 
magic users the title of "D."

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.220
I've never heard of it.

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:13.140
Your mother probably hadn't 
taught you about them yet.

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:16.920
Not all of the rumors about them are good.

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:19.710
So he's from this association?

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:24.060
<i>I cannot say for certain, but it is possible.</i>

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:26.630
But would a magic-user do something

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:29.840
to make his affiliation 
and status so obvious?

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:35.270
<i>It may be that he's so powerful, 
it makes no difference if he does.</i>

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:46.580
Does Sakura-san know?

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:49.590
<i>She hasn't said anything, 
and I haven't told her.</i>

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:51.660
Which means...

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:57.170
It is a power that Sakura-san cannot 
detect, but that you can.

00:10:57.610 --> 00:11:00.190
So he has Moon magic, too?

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:03.060
<i>It would be reasonable to assume so.</i>

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:07.960
<i>In which case, if anything happens,</i>

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:10.820
<i>it may be problematic for you,</i>

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.970
<i>as one who draws power 
from the same source.</i>

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:21.020
<i>You said nothing about the transfer 
student seemed unusual, yes?</i>

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:24.400
Right. She has no magic, 
and nothing about her seems off.

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:29.630
<i>Perhaps not, but she did move into 
the house in which I once lived.</i>

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:35.660
<i>Someone with the same type of magic 
power may have made that choice.</i>

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:40.290
<i>It's an ideal location for preserving 
people with magical power.</i>

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:43.280
You're saying they chose the 
house, knowing that?

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.250
<i>It is possible.</i>

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:49.760
I'll look into it on my end, as well.

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:52.480
I'll contact you if I find anything.

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:55.360
Thanks.

00:11:56.980 --> 00:12:01.780
<i>Of course. It's all to help Sakura-san 
and the people she holds dear.</i>

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:08.360
Another magic-user showed 
up near Sakura-chan?

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:10.750
For whatever reason,

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:14.610
those with great magical power 
converge around Sakura-san.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:16.200
And that's...

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:20.950
Because she possesses immense power herself.

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:25.000
Sakura-san is strong.

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:28.260
No one knows that better than I.

00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:30.830
You're right.

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:37.500
Besides, she has someone with her 
who treasures her above all else.

00:12:47.650 --> 00:12:49.090
How's school going?

00:12:49.090 --> 00:12:50.000
Normal.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:52.000
That's all you ever say.

00:12:52.390 --> 00:12:53.410
You?

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:54.740
It's fun.

00:12:54.740 --> 00:12:56.350
But English is hard.

00:12:56.350 --> 00:12:57.850
And math, right?

00:12:57.850 --> 00:13:00.580
Actually, I like math a little more now.

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:03.860
The teacher's explanations are 
really easy to understand.

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:05.980
This is good...

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.190
Is something different from usual?

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:10.810
I put butter in it.

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:17.800
Now that you mention it, I can tell!

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:20.190
Can you really?

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:21.810
Yes, I can!

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:24.620
I can taste the richness, 
and a sort of softness, too.

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:26.810
You sound like a TV food critic.

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:29.320
I was giving you a compliment!

00:13:29.660 --> 00:13:33.270
I forgot. Dad said he'll be 
away again this weekend.

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:34.720
I see...

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:39.170
Oh! Dad already told me it was okay,

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:42.620
but I promised my friend 
I'd show her our library.

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:45.220
Fine, if Dad said it was okay.

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:49.020
I'll move some of the books against 
the wall, so you can walk through.

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:50.210
Thanks!

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:54.520
Thank you for dinner.

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:57.950
Good luck at work!

00:14:00.260 --> 00:14:03.180
Kero-chan, you can come down now!

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:09.400
Your brother left?

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:10.460
Yep.

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:13.120
Yukibunny said he was goin' out, too.

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:16.360
Yukito-san and you really are 
texting buddies now, huh?

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:17.200
Yep!

00:14:17.200 --> 00:14:22.770
He always sends pictures of tasty-looking 
food, just when I'm feelin' hungry.

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:23.740
Look!

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:29.110
He told me you send him lots 
of food pictures, too.

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:30.340
An eye for an eye...

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:31.530
Like this!

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:32.540
And this!

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:34.350
Man, I look so cool!

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:37.340
You're in all of them.

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:38.970
How did you take those?

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:41.480
Tomoyo gave me a remote-control 
button for the shutter.

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:45.280
That thing sure comes in handy! 
It's perfect for selfies!

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:52.620
You can eat the cupcakes on the table.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.850
They're from my brother's work.

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:56.810
Yay!

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:02.570
Yum!

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:03.890
Take my picture!

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:04.530
Sure.

00:15:12.730 --> 00:15:13.890
Somethin' wrong?

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:20.340
Is it another card?

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:22.530
Yeah.

00:15:26.510 --> 00:15:28.060
Wait! Sakura!

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:39.320
Tomoyo had to go somewhere 
with her mom today,

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:41.150
so she asked me to fill in.

00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:45.330
She said, on the off-chance that you 
had to get down to business,

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:48.580
I should have you put that 
on and film it with this!

00:15:53.210 --> 00:15:55.290
T-Tomoyo-chan...

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:01.410
Sure has been a long time since we 
came to Penguin Park at night.

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:04.820
It really has. A lot happened here, too.

00:16:04.820 --> 00:16:08.640
Like the King Penguin bein' 
flipped upside-down...

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:09.530
Yeah.

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:15.070
Wait... It <i>is</i> upside-down!

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.700
It'll end up on the news again!

00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:23.330
This little one's upside-down, too.

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:36.660
All the penguins are being 
turned upside-down!

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:50.980
Man, why is this happening?!

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:54.610
We gotta do something!

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:57.150
But how?

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:06.080
There! That smoky stuff!

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:08.650
So that's the thing playin' this crazy prank?

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:09.710
I think so.

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:10.380
All right!

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:12.850
Let's get close and turn it into a card!

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:13.890
Right!

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:16.480
<i>Release!</i>

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.600
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:33.490
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:34.490
<i>Sec—</i>

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:52.480
Th-Thanks, Kero-chan...

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:54.220
That was a heck of a scare!

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:57.060
But I guess if we get too 
close to this thing...

00:17:57.060 --> 00:17:59.260
It'll turn us upside-down, too.

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:02.040
And then, our heads will get 
cracked on the ground.

00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:04.430
That's gonna hurt. Talk about a nasty bump.

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:06.080
A bump? O-Oh, no.

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:07.570
So what to do?

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:12.960
We've gotta do something fast!

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:18.390
What should we do?

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:28.030
I've got it!

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:32.030
That's enough!

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:45.580
All right!

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:48.420
If you're airborne, it doesn't 
matter which way's up!

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:52.830
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:56.180
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:18:56.710 --> 00:18:57.580
<i>Secure!</i>

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:14.380
<b>Reversal</b>

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:14.650
"Reversal"?

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:18.290
Reversal.

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:20.600
Does exactly what it says, huh?

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:21.900
Y-Yeah.

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:25.930
Anyway, we gotta use that card 
to put everything back—

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:30.460
What happened here?

00:19:30.820 --> 00:19:32.390
Wow, this is crazy.

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:34.120
What is this?

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:35.890
Why's it upside-down?

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:46.280
<i>So then, you flew back home?</i>

00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:50.290
If we'd stayed any longer, 
someone would've seen us...

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:53.230
And everyone's into social 
network sites these days!

00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:54.550
<i>Don't worry.</i>

00:19:55.010 --> 00:19:58.600
<i>It doesn't look like you two 
were caught on film!</i>

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:00.820
<i>Turn on the TV and see.</i>

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:07.600
<b>Live    Tomoeda's 
Penguin Park</b>

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:07.600
<b>Playground Equipment Turned Upside-Down</b>

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:04.570
<i>Last night, in this quiet park,</i>

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:07.600
<i>an incident turned the playground 
equipment upside-down.</i>

00:20:09.230 --> 00:20:11.310
<i>According to those who discovered it,</i>

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:14.440
<i>the crime took place in a span 
of about twenty minutes,</i>

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:20.150
<b>Live    Tomoeda's 
Penguin Park</b>

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:20.150
<b>Playground Equipment Turned Upside-Down</b>

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:16.640
<i>but no one saw the responsible party.</i>

00:20:16.640 --> 00:20:19.200
<i>He or she is currently considered at large.</i>

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:20.100
<i>This concludes—</i>

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:24.550
It's big news now...

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:26.550
All because we ran in such a hurry.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:31.110
<i>It was the only way to keep 
the world from finding out</i>

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:33.500
<i>about the Cardcaptors.</i>

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:37.120
<i>When things settle down, 
we can go back to fix it!</i>

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:39.330
Y-You're right.

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:43.400
<i>And Kero-chan...</i>

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:44.130
Yeah?

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:46.730
<i>How did the video recording go?</i>

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:49.210
I got it all, of course!

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:51.910
<i>I'd love to see it.</i>

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:52.730
Sure!

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:04.240
This will let Tomoyo-chan see 
the same video as we do?

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:05.030
Yep!

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:06.970
Then we do this, and this.

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:08.740
All right, here goes...

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:10.240
Push the button.

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:23.920
It's making me dizzy!

00:21:28.610 --> 00:21:29.510
Huh?

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:31.930
What were you filming here?

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:33.600
Oh, this...

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:38.020
When you were first flipped upside-down, 
and I caught you in my mouth...

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:41.970
I guess the camera on my head slipped.

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:52.650
Well, accidents are bound to 
happen at any film location!

00:21:52.650 --> 00:21:54.030
<i>That's true.</i>

00:21:55.800 --> 00:21:58.480
<i>Irregularities are a part of filming.</i>

00:22:00.510 --> 00:22:01.680
<i>Kero-chan...</i>

00:22:05.430 --> 00:22:06.440
Yes?

00:22:06.440 --> 00:22:08.780
<i>Let's start special training tomorrow!</i>

00:22:09.810 --> 00:22:11.940
F-For what?

00:22:11.940 --> 00:22:14.540
<i>Video recording, of course!</i>

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:19.750
<i>We'll train so we'll never miss a second 
of Sakura-chan's efforts again!</i>

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:20.950
You...

00:22:20.950 --> 00:22:23.330
You seem very passionate about this.

00:22:23.330 --> 00:22:26.580
<i>Let's strive to become camera 
masters, together!</i>

00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:29.530
I don't really get it, but... Sure!

00:22:30.040 --> 00:22:31.750
Okay! So like this?

00:22:31.750 --> 00:22:32.840
<i>That looks great.</i>

00:22:32.840 --> 00:22:34.250
And then, maybe this...

00:22:34.250 --> 00:22:34.930
<i>Wonderful!</i>

00:22:34.930 --> 00:22:36.030
How 'bout this?

00:22:36.030 --> 00:22:36.980
<i>Perfect!</i>

00:24:09.970 --> 00:24:12.390
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:15.510
Time for that magic moment, 
"Leave It to Kero-chan!"

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:17.720
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:17.720
<b>K</b>

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:18.740
Today, we'll be looking at the 
park that keeps showin' up!

00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:18.720
<b>I love that place.</b>

00:24:18.740 --> 00:24:20.630
Everyone calls it Penguin Park,

00:24:20.630 --> 00:24:22.450
but its official name is 
Tomoeda Central Park.

00:24:22.450 --> 00:24:24.840
It's a kids' playground, 
on a big green space.

00:24:24.840 --> 00:24:27.920
It has a penguin-shaped slide, 
nicknamed King Penguin,

00:24:27.920 --> 00:24:30.940
plus swings, see-saws, a jungle gym, 
and other playground equipment.

00:24:30.940 --> 00:24:33.310
It has lots of greenery, too, 
and the perfect location!

00:24:32.990 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:32.990 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>K</b>

00:24:33.310 --> 00:24:35.840
It's nice to just relax in 
a park, now and then.

00:24:35.840 --> 00:24:38.360
I'd like to take a nice nap 
in the park, myself.

00:24:38.360 --> 00:24:40.000
Ta-ta!

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.250
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:24:40.250 --> 00:24:42.240
It's my first ball-sports tournament.

00:24:42.240 --> 00:24:44.500
I love PE stuff, so I'm really excited!

00:24:44.500 --> 00:24:48.430
What? Akiho-chan and Syaoran-kun 
are facing off in badminton?!

00:24:48.430 --> 00:24:51.770
Next time, "Sakura and the Icy 
Ball-Sports Tournament."

00:24:49.130 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Sakura and the Icy Ball-Sports Tournament</b>

00:24:51.770 --> 00:24:55.010
Say it with me: "Release!"

00:24:55.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>End</b>
